{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.fundamental_passes_gate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.fundamental_passes_gate","kind":"theorem","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateMultiplicity.lean#L286-L288","doc":"The smallest object that does pass: the 2-dimensional fibre itself,\n`W = V_{1/2}`.  Consistent with `Sym2GateParity.fundamental_passes_gate`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.two_copies_fails_gate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.two_copies_fails_gate","kind":"theorem","line":284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateMultiplicity.lean#L284-L284","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.two_copies_dim_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.two_copies_dim_four","kind":"theorem","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateMultiplicity.lean#L278-L282","doc":"**Even dimension is necessary, not sufficient.**  `W = V_{1/2}^{⊕2}` has\neven dimension `4`, yet fails the gate: two copies of a symplectic irrep pair\ninto a singlet of `Sym²`.  Recorded so the parity invariant is not read as a\ncharacterisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.reducible_three_fails_gate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.reducible_three_fails_gate","kind":"theorem","line":275,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateMultiplicity.lean#L275-L276","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.reducible_three_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.reducible_three_dim","kind":"theorem","line":266,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateMultiplicity.lean#L266-L273","doc":"**The new content.**  `W = V_{1/2} ⊕ V_0` has dimension `3` and is\n**reducible**, so `Sym2GateParity.adjoint_fails_gate` — a statement about a\nsingle irrep — does not apply to it.  It fails the gate all the same: the\ntrivial summand `V_0` is orthogonal, and its own symmetric square is a singlet.\n\nThis is the case the irrep-level argument left open, and the reason the\nmultiplicity form is needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.single_irrep_gate_iff_not_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.single_irrep_gate_iff_not_even","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateMultiplicity.lean#L252-L264","doc":"**Consistency with `Sym2GateParity`.**  On a single irrep with multiplicity\none, the multiplicity criterion reproduces\n`Sym2GateParity.zero_mem_sym2Indices_iff`: the gate passes exactly when `2j` is\nodd, i.e. exactly when `dim V_j` is even.  So this file extends the companion\ncriterion rather than competing with it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.sym2SingletCount_single","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.sym2SingletCount_single","kind":"theorem","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateMultiplicity.lean#L246-L250","doc":"The count on a single isotypic component. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.gate_fails_of_odd_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.gate_fails_of_odd_dim","kind":"theorem","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateMultiplicity.lean#L234-L242","doc":"The contrapositive, for any odd dimension: odd-dimensional objects fail the\ngate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.dimOfMult_ne_three_of_gate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.dimOfMult_ne_three_of_gate","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateMultiplicity.lean#L225-L232","doc":"**The exclusion the chapter needs.**  No three-dimensional object of the\nsingle-fibre category passes the `Sym²` gate — irreducible or not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.even_dimOfMult_of_gate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.even_dimOfMult_of_gate","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateMultiplicity.lean#L218-L223","doc":"**The invariant, stated as parity.**  Any object passing the `Sym²` gate has\neven dimension. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.two_dvd_dimOfMult_of_gate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.two_dvd_dimOfMult_of_gate","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateMultiplicity.lean#L200-L216","doc":"Every term of `dim W` is even once the gate passes: the orthogonal terms\nvanish outright, and the symplectic ones carry the even factor `2j + 1` with\n`2j` odd. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.sym2SingletCount_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.sym2SingletCount_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateMultiplicity.lean#L172-L196","doc":"**The gate, for an arbitrary object.**  `Sym²(W)` has no singlet exactly\nwhen `W` contains no orthogonal (odd-dimensional) irrep at all, and contains\neach symplectic (even-dimensional) irrep at most once.\n\nEquivalently: a passing `W` is a direct sum of **pairwise distinct\neven-dimensional** irreps. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.choose_two_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.choose_two_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateMultiplicity.lean#L164-L168","doc":"A symplectic isotypic component contributes no singlet exactly when its\nmultiplicity is at most one — two copies of a symplectic irrep already pair up\nto a singlet in `Sym²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.choose_two_succ_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.choose_two_succ_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateMultiplicity.lean#L159-L162","doc":"An orthogonal isotypic component contributes no singlet exactly when it is\nabsent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.sym2SingletCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.sym2SingletCount","kind":"def","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateMultiplicity.lean#L145-L155","doc":"The number of singlets in `Sym²(W)`, by the Frobenius–Schur count.\n\nAn orthogonal irrep (`2j` even, `FS = +1`) has a **symmetric** invariant form,\nso its isotypic component contributes `Sym²` of the multiplicity space,\n`C(m+1, 2)`.  A symplectic irrep (`2j` odd, `FS = −1`) has an **antisymmetric**\none, contributing `Λ²`, `C(m, 2)`.\n\nThis definition *is* the model: the Clebsch–Gordan decomposition and the\nindicator are cited from the literature, not derived here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.dimOfMult","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.Sym2GateMultiplicity.dimOfMult","kind":"def","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/Sym2GateMultiplicity.lean#L142-L143","doc":"`dim W = Σ_j m_j · (2j + 1)`, since `dim V_j = 2j + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}